IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il41-nouns`
IMPORT `il41-opinions`
IMPORT `il41-representation`

-- TESTS for Chapter B (ss 6 to 12), written from the text (Sefer HaChukim 3550 pp. 803-804) before the modules were run.
-- Hand rules: s 12(a) takes three things out of the Chapter (criminal-law proceedings; powers an enactment gave the Attorney General; representation of bodies exercising judicial or quasi-judicial
-- power); s 12(b) keeps s 7 for an executive party; s 7 fixes the position (the Government, else the Attorney General); s 9 lets the Government choose another lawyer where the Attorney General has
-- given notice (s 8) or the minister concerned considers the position is not properly presented; s 10(a) bars the Attorney General from appearing then without approval; s 11 needs consent.

§ `Tests: Chapter B`

-- s 12(a): arguments are: criminal-law proceeding, statutory power, judicial body.
#ASSERT `Chapter B applies to the matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Chapter B applies to the matter` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Chapter B applies to the matter` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Chapter B applies to the matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 12(b): arguments are: criminal-law proceeding, statutory power, judicial body, the executive authority is a party.
#ASSERT `s 7 applies to the matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7 applies to the matter` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7 applies to the matter` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7 applies to the matter` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7 applies to the matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `who fixes the position of the executive authority` TRUE EQUALS `the Government, by a position it has determined`
#ASSERT `who fixes the position of the executive authority` FALSE EQUALS `the Attorney General, where the Government has determined none`

-- ss 6, 8, 9: arguments are: criminal-law, statutory power, judicial body, notice under s 8, minister concerned considers, Government has decided.
#ASSERT `who presents the position of the executive authority` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `another lawyer whom the Government has chosen`
#ASSERT `who presents the position of the executive authority` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `another lawyer whom the Government has chosen`
#ASSERT `who presents the position of the executive authority` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the Attorney General`
#ASSERT `who presents the position of the executive authority` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the Attorney General`
#ASSERT `who presents the position of the executive authority` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the Attorney General`
#ASSERT `who presents the position of the executive authority` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `who presents the position of the executive authority` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `who presents the position of the executive authority` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the body s 9 leaves to decide how the other lawyer is paid` EQUALS `the Government`

-- s 10: arguments are: another lawyer chosen, the proceeding touches the criminal-law domain, the approval.
#ASSERT `s 10(a) lets the Attorney General appear` TRUE FALSE `no approval` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 10(a) lets the Attorney General appear` TRUE FALSE `approval of the Government` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10(a) lets the Attorney General appear` TRUE FALSE `approval of a ministerial committee` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10(a) lets the Attorney General appear` TRUE FALSE `approval of the Minister of Justice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10(a) lets the Attorney General appear` TRUE FALSE `approval given in another way the Government determined` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10(a) lets the Attorney General appear` FALSE FALSE `no approval` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10(a) lets the Attorney General appear` TRUE TRUE `no approval` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 11: arguments are: the kind of body, the Attorney General consents, the body consents, the Knesset's legal adviser consents.
#ASSERT `s 11 lets the Attorney General represent the body` `the Knesset` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11 lets the Attorney General represent the body` `the Knesset` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 11 lets the Attorney General represent the body` `another body of the State outside the executive` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11 lets the Attorney General represent the body` `another body of the State outside the executive` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 11 lets the Attorney General represent the body` `another body of the State outside the executive` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 11 lets the Attorney General represent the body` `the Government` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11 lets the Attorney General represent the body` `an incorporated body` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11 lets the Attorney General represent the body` `a court` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
